Option (b) would REJECT worktree folders whose manifest id has stray whitespace — harsher UX; also `WidgetManifest.fromJson` itself trims, so downstream treats " fa-agents " as "fa-agents". Chrome-parity suggests lenient trim. I choose trim-at-source: make `UnpackedInspection.id` (the loader's view) return the trimmed id — the single point both the flow and the loader consume. Additionally, to keep the validator's contract coherent ("the destination folder name under apps/"), I'll ALSO trim in `WidgetPayloadValidation.id` — no wait. Scope discipline (F4: don't refactor unrelated code). `WidgetPayloadValidation.id` is consumed ONLY by `UnpackedInspection`. The reviewer pinned the fix on the loader. Minimal: trim in `UnpackedInspection.id` getter:

```dart
/// The manifest id — the destination folder name under `apps/`. Null
/// when the manifest never parsed (the load is refused anyway).
///
/// TRIMMED: the id rule runs against `id.trim()` (the same value
/// `WidgetManifest.fromJson` stores), so the folder the widget lands in
/// and every stored record carry the rule-enforced form — never
/// `apps/ fa-agents /` from a padded manifest.
String? get id => validation.id?.trim();
```

